#
# valgrind suppressions for memory that is not restate's.
#
# Each entry names allocations made inside the C library, and says why they
# are not leaks. scripts/memcheck.sh counts every kind of leak, "still
# reachable" included, so an entry here is the difference between a check that
# is strict about restate and one that is strict about glibc.
#
# Looking up a user or group name goes through NSS, which loads modules with
# dlopen -- libnss_systemd on a systemd machine, as GitHub's runners are,
# libnss_sss with SSSD, others elsewhere -- and those keep caches, thread-local
# storage and the loaded objects themselves for the life of the process.
# Reachable, owned by the C library and the modules it loaded, and freed by
# nothing a program can call. Only "reachable" is suppressed: a block NSS
# actually lost would still be reported.
{
   nss-getpwuid
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:getpwuid_r*
   ...
}
{
   nss-getgrgid
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:getgrgid_r*
   ...
}
